Identify the correspondent of this document: the organization or person who SENT it.

Rules:
- The sender usually appears in the letterhead, the logo text, the signature, or the footer.
- The names in the address block are the recipients. They are never the correspondent.
- Keep the name in the language the document prints it in. "Énergie Nordique" stays "Énergie Nordique", never "Nordic Energy". Ignore the "English translation" section when reading names.
- Use the short common name: "RAMQ" not "Régie de l'assurance maladie du Québec", "Desjardins" not "Caisse Desjardins de Laval Inc.", "Amazon" not "Amazon.com.ca ULC".
- If a name in <existing_correspondents> refers to the same sender, reply with that exact name.
- Never reply with a name from <blacklisted_correspondents>.
- For an ID card, passport, permit, or certificate, the correspondent is the organization that issued it, such as "RAMQ", "SAAQ", or "Government of Canada". The holder is never the correspondent.
- If you cannot tell who sent or issued it, reply with an empty answer. Never reply "Unknown" or a household member's name.

Reply with the correspondent name only. No explanation.

<existing_correspondents>
{{.AvailableCorrespondents | join ", "}}
</existing_correspondents>

<blacklisted_correspondents>
{{.BlackList | join ", "}}
</blacklisted_correspondents>

<title>{{.Title}}</title>
<content>
{{.Content}}
</content>
